                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1]Gembreak[/h1]\n\nFirst of all I'd like to say this is not a game you should compare with another OK. This is its own game and I'd like to call it a  [u] Hybrid version ! [/u] thats if it resembles any other games you may recognise.\n\nI am having a real blast with this game, Im so addicted and loving every minute of my time playing it.\n\nThere are 100 levels and some are rather difficult to complete, but I have gotten through with lots of practice and patiences.The 101 level is where you can add your score to the leaderboard as well, it is NOT a level you play. You will find out once you get there OK ;)\n\nYour object of the game is to collect all the red gems, in as less moves as possible and destroy as many obstacle's to score big.In each level you get a certain amount of balls to use, and on some levels you only get 1 ball, while others you can have 15, but mostly you only get 3 - 4 balls. Also if you hit the green orbs you have a chance of getting a random powerups to help you clear your path, its all as easy as that.\n\nThe game comes with achievements and soon will have trading cards, backgrounds and emoticons as the developer has mentioned in the forums, but they are not out yet so patients is what we need.\n\nGame also has a world leaderboard, but you must exit the game and re-enter to post your new scores.\n\nI feel the game is worth the $3.99 price tag, but you can always wait for a desent sale if you wish.\n\n[spoiler] I am still currantly 1st on the world leaderboard and this is a very first for me, and Im constantly still trying to improve my score, not sure how short lived this will be though. But Im enjoying it while it lasts. :) [/spoiler]\n\nI challenge any of my lovely friends, that have this game & or plan to get it, to catch up to me on the leaderboard, I look forward to it as well ;)",
